#!/bin/sh
# Pre-push hook — intentionally a no-op.
#
# HISTORY: this hook enforced the pre-ship simulator gate (blocked a push to main
# containing mobile/src changes unless qa/sim-runs/last-sim-run.json recorded a passing
# Maestro run on an ancestor of the pushed commit), and warned when mobile/src/screens/
# changed without a matching capture under screens/.
#
# D-056 (2026-08-15) retired Maestro and the simulator ENTIRELY — no flow authoring, no
# flow execution, no screens/ captures, for any change in any pipeline. That made both
# checks unsatisfiable: the gate could only ever be passed via FTF_SKIP_SIM_GATE=1, which
# became the standing posture, and the freshness warning told you to run a capture that
# policy forbids. A gate that is always overridden is not a gate; it just trains people to
# ignore hook output. So it is gone rather than left firing.
#
# The gate's replacement is CI plus recorded evidence, not a local hook:
#   - CI: backend-tests, mobile-typecheck (also runs the mobile/tests/check-*.js suites),
#     maestro-testid-lint  (testIDs still matter; the lint outlived the flows)
#   - Evidence: living-memory/TEST_LEDGER.md, and a manual TestFlight checklist when
#     runtime proof matters
#   - See docs/templates/feature-scope.md §3 and §5.
#
# FTF_SKIP_SIM_GATE is no longer read. Leaving it set is harmless.
#
# This file is kept (rather than deleted) so that `git config core.hooksPath githooks`
# stays valid for clones that already set it. Add real pre-push checks here if you ever
# want them — but do not restore a gate that has to be overridden to push.

exit 0
